# KiCad generated, per-user, and disposable state.
# See hardware/README.md for what belongs in git and why.

# Autosave archives — KiCad writes one zip per save. This is the single
# biggest source of bloat in the original folders (~1.9 GB across the tree).
*-backups/
_autosave-*
*.bak
*.bak2

# Footprint cache — several MB per project, regenerated by KiCad on demand.
fp-info-cache

# Per-user GUI state (open sheet, zoom, active layer). Churns on every open
# and carries no design information.
*.kicad_prl

# Lock files left behind by open or crashed KiCad sessions.
*.lck

# KiCad's built-in local-history repos.
.history/

# 3D and mechanical exports: large, binary, and re-exportable from the board.
# Commit deliberately with `git add -f` if a specific one is worth keeping.
*.step
*.stp
*.3mf
*.wrl

# ...except the vendored part models. Those are INPUTS, not exports -- the
# footprints reference them, and without them the 3D view is broken for
# everyone who is not on the machine the boards were drawn on. See
# 3dmodels/README.md.
!3dmodels/
!3dmodels/**

# Netlist/BOM/plot exports — regenerate with kicad-cli, see README.
*.net
*.xml

# Fab output. Generated from the board at order time; the git tag on that
# commit is the record of what was sent, not a checked-in copy. The empty
# gerbers/ directories are kept as the conventional export target.
# (A pattern with an embedded slash is anchored to this file's directory, so
# `gerbers/*` alone would only match hardware/gerbers/ — hence the `**/`.)
**/gerbers/*
!**/gerbers/.gitkeep
*.bak-*
